  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Women Economic Opportunities in Jordan Operation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the Enhancing Women&apos;s Economic Opportunities in Jordan Operation for Jordan is to address constraints that women face to enter and stay in the labor force related to the workplace conditions, financial inclusion, transportation, and childcare. The economic modernization vision (EMV) (2023-2033) presents two strategic pillars: (i) accelerated growth through unleashing Jordan&apos;s full economic potential; and (ii) improved quality of life for all citizens and sets a target to double women&apos;s economic participation by 2033. To operationalize the overarching objectives, the Government of Jordan (GOJ) has identified a series of priority initiatives in the engendered strategy action plan as an integrated part of the overall EMV executive program (2023-2025). The operation will support the implementation of the EMV engendered strategy and its priority actions under four main areas: (i) legislative reforms and gender seal, (ii) women e-shops and providing financing and non-financial support to women, (iii) public transport planning and solutions for women, and (iv) expanding quality nurseries.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To increase women&apos;s economic opportunities by creating a more enabling environment and facilitating women&apos;s entry into the labor market by addressing key constraints such as childcare. (TBC)</narrative>
  </description>
